import "json/importer.ct"
import "python/importer.ct"


# # The importers the standard library supplies
  A file reached without an import line above it — one the compiler was given to compile, or one
  found in the listing of a directory — has no page to look on for the importer that reads it. This
  is the page it looks on instead: the importers a program gets without asking for them.
  It declares none itself and imports the pages that do, so that finding an importer here is the
  same act as finding one among a file's own imports. One rule, in one place.
  It is deliberately not under @core/@, and nothing under @core/@ may import it. Naming an importer
  means importing the page declaring it, and every importer page imports @hsrawprgm()@ — so a
  registry the standard library reached would put the whole of the compiler's own syntax into every
  program.
